{
  "page": 4,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "conservatism cannot be eliminated, but it should be avoided. Therefore, our goal is not just to",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        94.42461395263672,
        522.0001831054688,
        104.17735290527344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "compute an ϵ-accurate reachable set, but to compute an ϵ-accurate reachable set with as small a",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        107.79907989501953,
        522.0033569335938,
        117.72636413574219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "volume as possible.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        121.52263641357422,
        175.53826904296875,
        131.27537536621094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This goal can be stated as a chance-constrained optimization problem:",
      "bbox": [
        106.93603515625,
        135.0716552734375,
        413.2416076660156,
        144.8243865966797
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimize",
      "bbox": [
        222.87002563476562,
        155.8896484375,
        264.0845642089844,
        165.6423797607422
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ",
      "bbox": [
        241.384033203125,
        165.2327880859375,
        245.3372039794922,
        172.31024169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Vol( ˆR[t0,t1](θ))",
      "bbox": [
        274.9520263671875,
        152.95709228515625,
        342.5613708496094,
        167.7726287841797
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subject to",
      "bbox": [
        222.87005615234375,
        178.77667236328125,
        264.9900817871094,
        188.52940368652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PZ( ˆR[t0,t1](θ)) ≥1 −ϵ",
      "bbox": [
        274.9520568847656,
        175.8450927734375,
        379.1682434082031,
        190.65965270996094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(2)",
      "bbox": [
        509.2801513671875,
        166.99969482421875,
        522.0001831054688,
        176.75242614746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This optimization problem is intractable in general. However, in certain cases we may approxi-",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        198.55169677734375,
        522.0003662109375,
        208.30442810058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mately solve this problem using scenario optimization, arriving at a probabilistically guaranteed",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        212.1007080078125,
        521.9986572265625,
        221.8534393310547
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Monte Carlo approach to estimating the reachable set.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        225.64971923828125,
        325.71295166015625,
        235.40245056152344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Scenario Optimization",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        255.39599609375,
        220.18032836914062,
        266.1437072753906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Scenario optimization is a technique to approximately solve optimization problems of the form",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        276.9977111816406,
        504.349365234375,
        286.75042724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimize",
      "bbox": [
        223.64414978027344,
        296.9667053222656,
        264.85870361328125,
        306.71942138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ",
      "bbox": [
        242.15814208984375,
        306.309814453125,
        246.11131286621094,
        313.38726806640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "J(θ)",
      "bbox": [
        275.72613525390625,
        296.7921447753906,
        296.73577880859375,
        306.47943115234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subject to",
      "bbox": [
        223.64413452148438,
        319.00469970703125,
        265.76416015625,
        328.7574157714844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PZ(g(θ, Z) ≤0) ≥1 −ϵ",
      "bbox": [
        275.72613525390625,
        318.21923828125,
        388.35626220703125,
        329.6362609863281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ ∈Θ,",
      "bbox": [
        275.7261657714844,
        334.7572326660156,
        306.0018615722656,
        345.055419921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(3)",
      "bbox": [
        509.2801513671875,
        316.272705078125,
        522.0001831054688,
        326.0254211425781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where J and g are convex functions, Θ ∈Rnθ is convex and compact, and PZ is a probability",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        352.69268798828125,
        521.9954833984375,
        366.6864013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "measure with respect to a random variable Z. Solving (3) directly is an intractable problem because",
      "bbox": [
        90.0001220703125,
        368.6201477050781,
        522.0050659179688,
        378.54742431640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the probabilistic constraint is difﬁcult to enforce for general random variables, and is not guaranteed",
      "bbox": [
        90.00010681152344,
        382.3437194824219,
        522.0003662109375,
        392.096435546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to be convex even when g is a convex.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00010681152344,
        395.7181701660156,
        256.3177795410156,
        405.64544677734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Scenario optimization proceeds by solving a deterministic approximation of the problem:",
      "bbox": [
        106.93612670898438,
        409.4417419433594,
        496.5980224609375,
        419.1944580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "minimize",
      "bbox": [
        214.54812622070312,
        429.4107360839844,
        255.7626953125,
        439.1634521484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ",
      "bbox": [
        233.0621337890625,
        438.75384521484375,
        237.0153045654297,
        445.831298828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "J(θ)",
      "bbox": [
        266.630126953125,
        429.2361755371094,
        287.6387939453125,
        438.9234619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subject to",
      "bbox": [
        214.5481414794922,
        452.4467468261719,
        256.6681823730469,
        462.199462890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "g(θ, z(i)) ≤0,",
      "bbox": [
        266.630126953125,
        449.807861328125,
        329.5358581542969,
        461.95947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i = 1, . . . , N",
      "bbox": [
        339.4958801269531,
        452.2721862792969,
        396.27587890625,
        461.95947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ ∈Θ,",
      "bbox": [
        266.6301574707031,
        468.19927978515625,
        296.9058532714844,
        478.4974670410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(4)",
      "bbox": [
        509.2801513671875,
        449.2147521972656,
        522.0001831054688,
        458.96746826171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where {z(i)}N",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        489.0148620605469,
        152.9009552001953,
        500.8604736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1 are N independently and identically-distributed (iid) samples from Z. This prob-",
      "bbox": [
        146.18215942382812,
        490.9331970214844,
        521.99853515625,
        503.9164733886719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lem is a non-probabilistic convex program, and so can be solved efﬁciently even in the general case",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        504.65771484375,
        522.0003662109375,
        514.4104614257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by a range of standard solvers.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        518.206787109375,
        223.1348114013672,
        527.9595336914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Scenario optimization approach proposes that the minimizer of (4), which we can easily",
      "bbox": [
        106.9361572265625,
        531.7557373046875,
        522.0053100585938,
        541.5084838867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬁnd, is also a feasible solution of (3) with high probability. Furthermore, there is a lower bound on",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        545.3047485351562,
        522.0003051757812,
        555.0574951171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this probability with respect to N:",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        558.67919921875,
        239.04388427734375,
        568.6065063476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Theorem 1 (Tempo et al. (2012), Corollary 12.1) let δ ∈(0, 1). If N is selected according to",
      "bbox": [
        90.00015258789062,
        579.7402954101562,
        507.3495178222656,
        590.2021484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N ≥1",
      "bbox": [
        232.23513793945312,
        599.63916015625,
        263.38470458984375,
        616.7064819335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ϵ",
      "bbox": [
        258.4440002441406,
        614.5020751953125,
        262.87310791015625,
        624.1893920898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
